    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\r\n\r\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\r\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\r\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\r\n\r\n### Module(s)\r\n\r\nmini.pick\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\nSince commit 42100d8,  the `grep_live` function does not show any item to pick from when using the `rg` tool.  \r\n\r\nThe bug seems to be introduced by ` '--field-match-separator=\\\\0'` argument added on line 3224 (in pick.lua): applying \r\n[42100d8_patch.txt](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/16315694/42100d8_patch.txt) patch is fixing the problem.\r\n\r\n### Neovim version\r\n\r\n0.10.0\r\n\r\n### Steps to reproduce\r\n\r\n1. `echo \"foo\" > bar && nvim bar`\r\n2. Run comand `:lua require('mini.pick').builtin.grep_live({ tool = 'rg' })`\r\n3. Type \"foo\"\r\n\r\n### Expected behavior\r\n\r\n   - match line `bar:1:1:foo` is shown\r\n   - Info view indicates:\r\n   ```\r\n   Total items   | 1\r\n   Matched items | 1\r\n   Marked items  | 0\r\n   Current index | 1\r\n   ```\r\n\r\n### Actual behavior\r\n\r\n   - no match\r\n   - Info view indicates:\r\n   ```\r\n   Total items   | 0\r\n   Matched items | 0\r\n   Marked items  | 0\r\n   Current index | -\r\n   ```",
