        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> > Minimal supported version seems to be [13.0.0](https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep/releases/tag/13.0.0), which is 3 years old. I think it is old enough to not even be documented.\r\n> \r\n> Ubuntu 20.04 LTS package repository is [pointing at 11.0.2](https://packages.ubuntu.com/focal/utils/ripgrep). You're right, it's old, but still supported until April 2025: might happen to other users.\r\n\r\nI see, thanks for clarifying.\r\n\r\nAlthough there is nothing wrong in keep using something that is not broken, I think trying to support only the latest LTS version is a better approach here (as is the case with 'mini.deps' and 'mini.diff' which have explicit Git version check to make it work on Ubuntu 22.04). \r\n\r\nBesides, in this particular case there is no reasonable way to support both \":\" and \"\\0\" delimiters. Making breaking change is painful, but I believe is necessary here.",
