        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I was bit by this today when I upgraded Mini. While I saw the breaking change notices, I was expecting something different, but it did not work. Had I not been subscribed to all mini issues/discussions/etc... I would not have realized it was my version of `rg`, which was this btw:\r\n\r\n```\r\nripgrep 13.0.0\r\n-SIMD -AVX (compiled)\r\n+SIMD +AVX (runtime)\r\n```\r\n\r\nSo, I upgraded and life was good again.\r\n\r\n```\r\nripgrep 14.1.0\r\n\r\nfeatures:-simd-accel,+pcre2\r\nsimd(compile):+SSE2,+SSSE3,-AVX2\r\nsimd(runtime):+SSE2,+SSSE3,+AVX2\r\n\r\nPCRE2 10.42 is available (JIT is available)\r\n```\r\n",
